 least a month with a lower body injury, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-10-08T12:01:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50128461/brigham-young-tailback-lj-martin-least-month","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"BYU star RB Martin, LB Glasker to sit out Friday vs. Iowa State","description":"BYU will be without running back LJ Martin and linebacker Isaiah Glasker for Friday's game against Iowa State.","published":"2026-10-07T04:54:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50122325/byu-star-rb-martin-lb-glasker-sit-friday-vs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"BYU RB Martin exits vs. TCU after apparent first-half injury","description":"BYU running back LJ Martin was out of the No. 10 Cougars' game at TCU after suffering an apparent injury Saturday night.","published":"2026-10-04T04:01:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50095579/byu-rb-lj-martin-exits-vs-tcu-apparent-first-half-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918126/lj-martin","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LJ_Martin"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"LJ Martin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LJ_Martin","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:23Z","intro":"LJ Martin is an American college football running back for the BYU Cougars.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Martin attended Canutillo High School in Canutillo, Texas, where he rushed for 2,137 yards and 23 touchdowns and made 15 catches for 376 yards and six touchdowns as a senior. He was rated as a four-star recruit and received offers from schools such as BYU, Stanford, Texas Tech, Air Force, Baylor, Kansas, Kansas State, and Colorado State. Initially, Martin committed to play college football for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. However, he flipped his commitment to play for the Stanford Cardinal. Finally on signing day, Martin again flipped his commitment to the BYU Cougars."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"During Martin's first collegiate game in week one of the 2023 season he rushed for 91 yards on 16 carries, as he helped the Cougars to a win over the Sam Houston State. In week 3, Martin rushed for 77 yards and two touchdowns in a win over the Arkansas Razorbacks. Martin finished his first collegiate season rushing for 518 yards and four touchdowns on 109 carries, while also hauling in 11 receptions for 45 yards and one touchdown."}]}}